d no unrelated platform changes were recorded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f2af01787cc1423e","cmd-dff7d362eb6d4f86","cmd-9e6a639c5fdf4cef","cmd-d0ceed467cbb4706","cmd-6de8468f291d4a6f","cmd-09d550f4f9384614","cmd-ce886fed608e4bd3","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Direct scheduled transitions demonstrate synchronization well inside the 15-minute bound, including after sequential restarts. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service and data state, corroborated by the fixed lifecycle observations.","limitations":["The legacy platform does not support the lifecycle collector's systemd failed-unit probe; service recovery was instead observed directly through running cron and SSH processes, listening SSH sockets, authenticated access, checksums, and scheduled synchronization.","The propagation guarantee was tested with two bounded configuration changes rather than every possible edit pattern."]}
